{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"frankenstein complex frankenstein complex","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md","fileName":"Frankenstein Complex.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Frankenstein Complex","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","AI Narrative","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"frankenstein complex frankenstein complex","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Frankenstein Complex.md","fileName":"Frankenstein Complex.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Frankenstein Complex","heading":"Frankenstein Complex","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Frankenstein complex is the fear that an artificial creation will escape control and turn against its creator. In AI discourse it appears in stories about robots, autonomous weapons, and intelligent systems that become powerful enough to threaten humanity.\n\nThe narrative can be read as more than fear of a monster. Frankenstein also concerns a creator who fails to care for or accept responsibility for what he made. Applied to AI, this shifts attention from the imagined evil of the machine to the responsibilities of designers and institutions. It connects an [[AI Narrative]] to the practical problem of [[Algorithmic Accountability]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","AI Narrative","Algorithmic Accountability","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":